# 🛰️ Semantic Search — AIML Module

Satellite tiles ko text query se search karne ka module. CLIP (OpenAI) model se har tile ka embedding banaya jata hai, FAISS se fast search hota hai.

## File

- **`Semantic_Search_Clean.ipynb`** — Google Colab notebook. Isi mein sab kuch hai: model load karna, embeddings banana, index banana/save karna, aur search karna.

## Kaise chalao

1. Colab mein notebook kholo.
2. Runtime → Change runtime type → **T4 GPU** select karo → Save.
3. Step 2 mein `base_path` apne Drive ke tiles folder ke hisaab se set karo:
   ```
   base_path = Path("/content/drive/MyDrive/<tumhara_folder>/dataset/tiles")
   ```
4. **Runtime → Run all** karo.

⚠️ Pehli baar chalane pe embeddings banane mein 10-20 min lagte hain (Step 6). Ye Drive pe save ho jata hai (Step 6B), isliye **agli baar dobara nahi banana padta** — sirf Step 6C chalao (usme se `#` hata ke) jo saved index seconds mein load kar deta hai.

## Pre-built index (Google Drive)

Embeddings, FAISS index, `paths.pkl`, aur `search_results.json` already ban chuke hain — dobara build karne ki zarurat nahi (bahut bhari files hain, isliye GitHub pe nahi daali):

https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ahBTCmtxRgngz6OUUb08c4rEJDcofKZQ?usp=sharing

Backend team seedha yahan se `embeddings.npy`, `faiss.index`, `paths.pkl` download/use kar sakti hai, ya notebook ke Step 6C se load kar sakti hai.

## Input

`dataset/tiles/<City>/<year>/<tile_id>.tif` — Member 2 ke pipeline se aaya hua data. Har tile 256×256 px, 7 bands (B02, B03, B04, B08, B11, B12, valid).

## Output

- **Index files** (Drive pe save hote hain): `embeddings.npy`, `paths.pkl`, `faiss.index`
- **Search function**: `search_similar("query text", top_k=5)` — matching tiles ki list deta hai, images ke saath (Colab mein dikhta hai)
- **JSON export**: `search_to_json("query text", top_k=5)` — backend integrate karne ke liye

Example JSON output:
```json
{
  "query": "construction site",
  "results": [
    {"rank": 1, "score": 0.24, "tile_id": "Mumbai_r06_c05", "city": "Mumbai", "year": "2020", "path": "..."}
  ]
}
```

## Jaanne layak baatein

- **Score (0.2-0.3 jaisa) normal hai.** CLIP model normal camera photos pe train hua hai, satellite imagery pe nahi — isliye confidence number chhota dikhta hai, lekin results sahi aate hain. Score ko "kitna best match hai baaki results se" ke hisaab se dekho, absolute number ki tarah nahi.
- Model **general-purpose CLIP** hai, satellite-specific model nahi. Bahut niche/specific queries pe accuracy kam ho sakti hai.

## Backend ke liye

`search_similar()` ya `search_to_json()` function ko FastAPI route mein import/copy karke use kiya ja sakta hai. Index already saved hai, dobara build karne ki zarurat nahi — bas load karke query bhejni hai.
